From 21d2181b1c2bda92a0ce5a0b1e6c73a7c31d38ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:40:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Matrix editor support and fix the build on the multitouch
 QMK fork

- matrix_pointing.c/.h: answer the Matrix editor on the VIA custom
  channel, keep the settings in the user EEPROM datablock and apply them
  (CPI, tap-to-click, tap term, rotation / inversion, acceleration,
  scroll, auto mouse layer) and reboot into BOOTSEL on request.
- config.h: DYNAMIC_KEYMAP_LAYER_COUNT 5 so the _MOUSE layer (layer 4) is
  part of the VIA keymap (the fork refuses to build with the default 4);
  wire DIGITIZER_MOUSE_TAP_DETECTION_TIMEOUT to the Matrix tap term.
- Build fixes for george-norton/qmk_firmware multitouch_experiment:
  use the fork's maxtouch driver (DIGITIZER_DRIVER = maxtouch) instead of
  the stale local copy, no comment after POINTING_DEVICE_DRIVER (the fork
  compares it without stripping whitespace), non-empty "url" in
  keyboard.json, current RGB / mouse keycode names.
- Settings per OS (revision 22): OS_DETECTION_ENABLE and
  MATRIX_POINTING_OS_PROFILES; the Mac set takes the last 64 bytes of the
  EEPROM from the end of the macro buffer (DYNAMIC_KEYMAP_EEPROM_MAX_ADDR),
  so the keymap does not move.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
